From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000002 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anton <fourth@devpins.org>
Date: Wed, 3 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sdm845-xiaomi-beryllium: force USB host mode

USB OTG / Type-C role switching is incomplete on SDM845 (EXTCON), so the
DWC3 controller never enters host mode on its own and the port stays a
USB peripheral. That makes a USB DAC (Chord Mojo 2) fail to enumerate
unless host mode is forced from userspace after every boot, which is
unreliable on beryllium (OTG is officially "Broken").

This device is used as a dedicated bit-perfect audio player feeding a USB
DAC, so pin the controller to host mode permanently in the device tree.

Trade-off: the USB-C port no longer acts as a peripheral while booted (no
USB charging, no adb / usb-networking). Fastboot from the bootloader is
unaffected.

The dr_mode property lives in the shared -common.dtsi, so this single
change covers both the EBBG and Tianma panel variants. The hunk locates
by context (the &usb_1_dwc3 node is the only dr_mode in this file), so the
line number is approximate and patch(1) resolves it by offset.

Signed-off-by: Anton <fourth@devpins.org>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845-xiaomi-beryllium-common.dtsi | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845-xiaomi-beryllium-common.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845-xiaomi-beryllium-common.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845-xiaomi-beryllium-common.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845-xiaomi-beryllium-common.dtsi
@@ -171,3 +171,3 @@
 &usb_1_dwc3 {
-	dr_mode = "peripheral";
+	dr_mode = "host";
 };
